OL,3,GNEWSAGCSE maths results disappointing,
OL,4,Asays deputy
OL,5,
OL,6,FTeachers and senior leaders will be
OL,7,Flooking at ways to improve on this
OL,8,Fyear's GCSE results after some scores
OL,9,Fwere "a little bit patchy," an
OL,10,Feducation boss has said.
OL,12,FA total of 624 students opened their
OL,13,Fresults on Thursday, with those in
OL,14,FGuernsey and Alderney achieving a 71.2%
OL,15,Fpass rate for grades 4 and above.
OL,17,FDeputy Paul Montague said this year's
OL,18,Fmaths grades, however, were
OL,19,F"disappointing" noting teachers and
OL,20,Fsenior leaders will "look at those
OL,21,Fresults really carefully".
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
